 ### Vectorized Amanatides and Woo Variant
-A vectorized variant simplifies the code by avoiding explicit branching for axis selection using vector operations and operator overloading. It computes `steps` (distance to next boundary in terms of number of steps) and uses `argmin` to find the axis. This approach works for arbitrary dimensions but is practically used in 2D and 3D [S23, unofficial].
